 Q(f'How many real solutions satisfy $\\sqrt{{x+{a}}}=x-{a}$?',1,f'The domain requires $x\\ge {a}$.|Squaring gives $x^2-({2*a+1})x+{a*a-a}=0$.|Its roots are $({2*a+1}\\pm\\sqrt{{{8*a+1}}})/2$; only the plus root meets $x\\ge {a}$.','Write the sign condition before squaring.|The right side of a square-root equation must be nonnegative.',[0,2,3],check=1),
