 Q(f'Positive integers x,y satisfy $x+y={s}$. What is the largest possible xy?',a*(a+1),f'The real bound is ${s*s}/4$, which is not an integer.|The closest integers are ${a}$ and ${a+1}$, achieving ${a*(a+1)}$.','Use the real bound, then enforce integrality.|The sum is odd, so equal integer sides are impossible.',[a*a,(a+1)**2,F(s*s,4)],check=max(x*(s-x) for x in range(1,s))),
