 Q(f'A trapezoid with bases ${2*a}$ and ${4*a}$ and height ${b}$ contains a triangle of base ${2*a}$ and the same height. What area remains outside that triangle?',2*a*b,f'The trapezoid area is ${3*a*b}$.|The triangle area is ${a*b}$; their difference is ${2*a*b}$.','Compute both areas with the same height.|The triangle is stated to lie inside the trapezoid.',[3*a*b,a*b,4*a*b],check=F((2*a+4*a)*b,2)-F(2*a*b,2)),
