 Q(f'How many axis-aligned squares of all sizes are in an ${n}$ by ${n}$ grid of unit squares?',n*(n+1)*(2*n+1)//6,f'A square of side s has $(n-s+1)^2$ positions.|Sum the square counts to get ${n*(n+1)*(2*n+1)//6}$.','Count separately by side length.|A larger square has fewer possible positions.',check=sum((n-s+1)**2 for s in range(1,n+1))),
 Q(f'Two parallel lines each contain ${a}$ marked points. How many triangles can be formed from three marked points?',comb(2*a,3)-2*comb(a,3),f'Choose any three of the ${2*a}$ points, then exclude the collinear triples on either line.|The result is $\\binom{{{2*a}}}3-2\\binom{{{a}}}3={comb(2*a,3)-2*comb(a,3)}$.','A valid triangle cannot have all vertices on one line.|Three selected points on just two parallel lines are otherwise noncollinear.',check=2*comb(a,2)*a),
