 Q(f'How many length-${n}$ binary strings avoid three consecutive ones?',sum('111' not in ''.join(map(str,q)) for q in product([0,1],repeat=n)),f'Classify by endings 0, 01, and 011.|For length at least 3, $f(k)=f(k-1)+f(k-2)+f(k-3)$, with $f(0)=1,f(1)=2,f(2)=4$.|This gives ${sum('111' not in ''.join(map(str,q)) for q in product([0,1],repeat=n))}$.','Keep enough state to track the current run of ones.|The allowed terminal runs have length 0, 1, or 2.',check=compositions(n+1,[1,2,3])),
